      "made_by": "user",
      "decision": "DATABASE DESIGN GATE PASSED. The user reviewed and approved the charge_gaps schema, its rationale and its index plan, with one change: the date column is renamed to gap_date.",
      "why": "A bare `date` would be the only non-descriptive date column in the schema (cf. charged_on, captured_date, charge_start_date_time) and is a Postgres col_name_keyword. The Go domain field stays ChargeGap.Date to avoid stuttering.",
      "covered_by": null
    },
    {
      "id": "G2",
      "at": "2026-08-15T13:55:00Z",
      "scope": "change",
      "made_by": "user",
      "decision": "idx_charge_gaps_account (account_id, gap_date DESC) is KEPT despite serving a notification feature that does not exist yet.",
      "why": "Leader flagged it as speculative on a table that stays tiny. The user chose to keep it rather than defer; it is cheap and the read pattern is declared in the design.",
      "covered_by": null
    }
